# === job-search-os — .gitignore ===
# Per JOBS-ADR-003 D1: this repo is a template engine, the person is the data.
# profile/ holds real user data in any working instance and must NEVER be committed —
# only the *.template.md files ship. This is belt-and-suspenders with the pre-commit
# scrub hook (hooks/pre-commit) and the categorical refusal in D1b.

# ---- USER DATA — never committed ----
profile/*.md
!profile/*.template.md
roles/active/*.md
roles/passed/*.md
!roles/active/.gitkeep
!roles/passed/.gitkeep
!roles/_TEMPLATE.md
pipeline/*.md
!pipeline/*.template.md
applications/*
!applications/README.md
*.docx
*.pdf
!docs/**/*.pdf

# ---- USER DATA — binary/image files can carry real content a text scrub can't see ----
# (a screenshot of an offer letter, a comp email) — never committed outside docs/.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.heic
*.webp
!docs/**/*.png
!docs/**/*.jpg
!docs/**/*.jpeg
!docs/**/*.gif
!docs/**/*.heic
!docs/**/*.webp

# ---- OS / editor cruft ----
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/

# ---- Node (generators/ is self-contained, D8) ----
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ---- Never, under any circumstances ----
.env*
**/secrets/**
*.pem
*.key

# generators/node_modules is per-machine (npm install), never committed
generators/node_modules/

# OPERATIONS.md holds Tim's own deployment details (which GitHub account/repo this
# instance publishes to) — never ships in the public template, same reasoning as profile/.
OPERATIONS.md
